---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ConceptDiagram from "../../components/ConceptDiagram.astro";
import DockerPipelineDiagram from "../../components/DockerPipelineDiagram.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <section class="hero container prose">
    <h1>About K8s Practice Lab</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      An open-source, portfolio-grade learning platform for <strong>Docker, containers, and Kubernetes</strong>.
      Built for consistent daily practice — share it, fork it, or host it on AWS.
    </p>

    <h2>What makes this resume-worthy</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Full stack learning product</strong> — Astro static site, browser simulators, progress tracking</li>
      <li><strong>Dual-path infrastructure</strong> — localhost kind cluster + Terraform AWS hosting</li>
      <li><strong>Real-world debugging</strong> — 6 troubleshooting scenarios (Docker + Kubernetes)</li>
      <li><strong>Containerization best practices</strong> — multi-stage builds, non-root, health checks</li>
      <li><strong>Open source</strong> — others can clone, run <code>make site-dev</code>, and practice for free</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Three modes, one repo</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Browser</strong> — Docker + kubectl simulators, modules, quizzes, troubleshoot hub</li>
      <li><strong>Localhost</strong> — kind cluster + 8 guided labs with real YAML</li>
      <li><strong>AWS</strong> — optional Terraform to host the site on S3 + CloudFront</li>
    </ul>

    <DockerPipelineDiagram />
    <ConceptDiagram />

    <h2>For contributors & learners</h2>
    <p>
      Clone the repo, run <code>make site-dev</code> for browser practice or <code>make docker-lab</code> +
      <code>make local-lab</code> for hands-on work. No paid cloud Kubernetes required.
    </p>

    <h2>Built in public</h2>
    <p>
      Open source on <a href="https://github.com/Jacob-Idolor/Pet_Projects">GitHub</a>.
      Fork it, host your own copy, improve it, share it.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
